  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0034_9baf4d84bf47.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 266px;\" /></p><p>Give:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p><p>Displacement is defined to be the change in position of an object. As we can see from the above figure, displacement will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"
